cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these notebooks, please cite the Letter given under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "Notebooks for Tails, Trails, and Transients: Comets, NEOs, and Supernovae in Rubin Early Data Preview 2"
abstract: >-
  Two Jupyter notebooks that reproduce one example of each science case in the Letter
  on the Rubin Science Platform: cometary activity (C/2024 G6), activity on an
  asteroid-designated object (2025 NC6), a trailed near-Earth object (2025 OP1), and a
  supernova (SN 2025nbh). One uses the Butler and JPL Horizons; the other finds the
  epochs from scratch with Ponder and Sorcha.
version: "1.0.0"
license: BSD-3-Clause
